<title>UK: RUGBY UNION-ENGLAND BEAT ITALY 54-21 IN TEST. [CORRECTED 09:50 GMT]</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-ENGLAND BEAT ITALY 54-21 IN TEST. [CORRECTED 09:50 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>England beat Italy 54-21 (halftime</p>
<p>28-0) in a one-off test at Twickenham on Saturday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>England - Tries: Andy Gomarsall (2), Jon Sleightholme,</p>
<p>Lawrence Dallaglio, Martin Johnson (Corrects from Simon Shaw), Tim Rodber, Chris Sheasby.</p>
<p>Penalties: Mike Catt (3). Conversions: Catt (5)</p>
<p>Italy - Tries: Paolo Vaccari. Alessandro Tronkon, Orazio</p>
<p>Olancio. Conversions: Diego Dominguez (3)</p>
</text>
